= Ecology — Simple =

'''Ecology''' is the science of how living things interact with one another and with the places where they live.

An ecologist might study how plants respond to drought, why one animal population grows or declines, or how organisms and nutrients interact in an [[Ecosystem|ecosystem]].

Scientists use observations, experiments and models. A pattern found in one forest or ocean may not apply everywhere.

Ecology helps explain nature, but scientific findings alone do not decide every policy or conservation choice.

